  "reviewProtocol": "Fresh review of six fixed start/middle/end native samples per result, original native motion excerpts, and prior native review records. Compared with MRNF corner, corner A, construction fixed calibration, residential common-centre 1K/2K and FastGS published reviews. Not blinded; not every motion frame scored. Cross-capture and native-versus-browser render differences limit fine ordering.",
  "scope": "One physical street-side partial patch. Both route videos expose a large unsupported black region; three independent lateral sweeps have cuts.",
  "observations": [
    {
      "category": "along",
      "score": 5,
      "observation": "Paired native route 0, 6 and 11.97s: the observed houses and street direction are recognizable, but a large black unsupported region occupies much of the moving view. This is not a clean road traverse."
    },
    {
      "category": "lateral",
      "score": 5,
      "observation": "Paired native lateral 0, 6 and 11.97s: house shapes stay more recognizable than in the older full residential patch, but tree, window and porch boundaries still haze or stretch. The extended profile earns no defensible whole-point stability gain."
    },
    {
      "category": "detail",
      "score": 6,
      "observation": "The right-hand 12K native view contains some crisper roof/porch texture than the 5K view, but window and vegetation smearing persists. The difference is too small and inconsistent for another whole detail point."
    },
    {
      "category": "artifacts",
      "score": 3,
      "observation": "Paired lateral samples retain translucent foliage, smeared road shadows and dark near-vehicle holes. More training does not remove the dominant defects; unsupported route views are not treated as recovered facades."
    },
    {
      "category": "coverage",
      "score": 2,
      "observation": "Only one physical facade band and a partial corridor are supported. Large black route regions are an explicit completeness failure for free street exploration; neither run supplies both sides or a completed block."
    }
  ],
  "comparisons": [
    "Direct paired comparison: left 5K, right 12K, with the same numerical path, FOV, frame timing and native render settings. Both receive 46/100; the small texture difference does not justify a quality winner.",
    "The 12K profile also changes learning-rate/refinement horizons, so this is not an isolated iteration-count experiment.",
    "Compared with common-centre 2K (48/100), some supported-house views are more coherent, but the much narrower delivered view coverage and black route regions lower the overall visual score."
  ],
